Reuse of formed immediate addresses — 2026-10-18

The first ordinary load/store must still follow its constant pointer offset
without an intervening effect or computation. After that matching access,
later accesses in the same machine block can use its base and displacement.
The pre-allocation SSA base is immutable. Every access and volatile event
stays; no fact crosses a guard split. Different first addresses and calls
before the first access do not qualify. Atomic accesses keep their path.
This is ordinary instruction selection, not a new certified rewrite.

Unchanged sources and kernel argv, 100000 calls per case:
Symbol           Before/call After/call GCC14/call Before bytes After bytes
theta                    195        171         94          824         728
pte_offset_map            55         55         23          288         288
folio_state               32         32          9          152         152
Three container and three TCG runs agree on the retained checksums. The
plugin reports no dropped or irregular blocks and uses disjoint executable
addresses. GCC counts are retained, not rerun. The array meets its 2x exit;
the record and helper do not. No latency or whole-kernel result is claimed.

The address fixture covers positive/negative and packed offsets, a call and
another address before the first access, and a guard split. Both target
profiles and O0/O2 are checked. Four native target/optimization executions
and one Clang control pass under strict alignment. The three library-only
reductions have no main; their executed-path check refusals remain non-PASS.
Targeted tests: 4 address, 1 ABI snapshot and 23 proof-required tests pass.
Combined acceptance passes 456 Rust suites: 3460 passed, zero failed, eight
ignored, plus Clippy, formatting and all six Lean steps. The 15 relevant
Python tests, spec pins and generated status check pass. The working tree is
shared and dirty; this is not clean-tree release acceptance.

